diff --git a/docs/api/sections/webhooks.md b/docs/api/sections/webhooks.md
index a4f48b5..3f0f3aa 100644
--- a/docs/api/sections/webhooks.md
+++ b/docs/api/sections/webhooks.md
@@ -159,3 +159,40 @@ __Response:__
 ```
 
 `request` and `response` can be `null` for deliveries that have not started yet or are still in progress. The delivery request headers omit the `X-Webhook-Signature` header.
+
+## Receiving deliveries
+
+When an event a webhook subscribes to happens on its board, we `POST` it to the webhook's `payload_url` once, and record how it went in the delivery log. Deliveries are never repeated: an endpoint hears about an event exactly once, whether it answers or not.
+
+__Request:__
+
+```
+POST /webhooks HTTP/1.1
+User-Agent: fizzy/1.0.0 Webhook
+Content-Type: application/json
+X-Webhook-Timestamp: 2025-12-05T19:36:35.401Z
+X-Webhook-Signature: 4f1e7c...
+```
+
+The body is the event, in the same shape the API uses elsewhere:
+
+```json
+{
+  "id": "03f5v9zkft4hj9qq0lsn9ohde",
+  "action": "card_closed",
+  "created_at": "2025-12-05T19:36:35.401Z",
+  "eventable": { "id": "03f5v9zkft4hj9qq0lsn9ohdb", "title": "Ship it", "...": "..." },
+  "board": { "id": "03f5v9zkft4hj9qq0lsn9ohcy", "name": "Fizzy", "...": "..." },
+  "creator": { "id": "03f5v9zjw7pz8717a4no1h8a7", "name": "David Heinemeier Hansson", "...": "..." }
+}
+```
+
+Webhooks pointing at Basecamp, Campfire, or Slack get a chat message instead of the full event, ready to post in a room.
+
+Verify that a delivery came from us by computing the `HMAC` using `SHA256` of the raw request body with the webhook's `signing_secret` and comparing it to `X-Webhook-Signature`.
+
+## Failures
+
+Any response outside the `2XX` range, and any endpoint we can't reach, counts as a failed delivery. Ten failures in a row within an hour deactivate the webhook: it stops receiving deliveries until it's reactivated with a `POST` to its activation endpoint. A single successful delivery clears the streak.
+
+Deliveries are kept for a week, then dropped from the log.
